module

public import TauCeti.LinearAlgebra.SymmetricAlgebra.DividedDifference
public import TauCeti.RepresentationTheory.SymmetricAlgebra.Basic

/-!
# Divided-difference operators of a linear group action

Let `ρ` be a representation of a group `G` on a module `M`, and let `g ∈ G` and `ℓ ∈ M` be such
that `m - ρ g m` is a multiple of `ℓ` for every `m`. If `ℓ` is a nonzerodivisor of `Sym M`, the
divided-difference operator `δ_g p = (p - g • p) / ℓ` of `SymmetricAlgebra.dividedDifference` is
linear not only over the coefficients, but over the whole invariant subalgebra `Sym(M)^G`, since
every invariant is fixed by `g`. This file bundles it as a `Sym(M)^G`-linear map.

The main example is a pseudoreflection. Let `ρ` be a representation on a vector space `V` over a
field `K`, and let `g` fix pointwise a hyperplane `ker ℓ`, cut out by a nonzero linear form `ℓ`.
Then `φ - g • φ` is a multiple of `ℓ` for every linear form `φ`, where `G` acts on `V*` by the
contragredient representation `Representation.dual`
(`Representation.sub_dual_apply_mem_span_singleton`, in `TauCeti.RepresentationTheory.Dual`).
Hence `g` has a divided-difference operator `δ_g f = (f - g • f) / ℓ` on the polynomial functions
`Sym(V*)`, which is linear over the polynomial invariants `Sym(V*)^G`, lowers degrees by one, and
satisfies the operator identity `1 - g = m_ℓ ∘ δ_g`. These operators are the basic tool of the
proof that the polynomial invariants of a finite group generated by pseudoreflections form a
polynomial algebra.

## Main definitions

* `Representation.symmetricAlgebraDividedDifference`: the divided-difference operator of `g`, as
  a linear map over the invariant subalgebra.

## References

* R. Kane, *Reflection Groups and Invariant Theory*, CMS Books in Mathematics, Springer (2001),
  §§ 17–18.
* L. Smith, *Polynomial Invariants of Finite Groups*, A K Peters (1995), § 7.2.
-/

public section

namespace Representation

section CommRing

variable {R G M : Type*} [CommRing R] [Monoid G] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
variable (ρ : Representation R G M) (g : G) (ℓ : M)

/-- The divided-difference operator `p ↦ (p - g • p) / ℓ` of `g` on `Sym M`, bundled as a linear
map over the invariant subalgebra `Sym(M)^G`. It requires `m - ρ g m` to be a multiple of `ℓ` for
every `m`, and `ℓ` to be a nonzerodivisor in `Sym M`. Its underlying map is
`SymmetricAlgebra.dividedDifference (ρ g) ℓ`. -/
noncomputable def symmetricAlgebraDividedDifference (hσ : ∀ m, m - ρ g m ∈ R ∙ ℓ)
    (hℓ : IsLeftRegular (SymmetricAlgebra.ι R M ℓ)) :
    SymmetricAlgebra R M →ₗ[ρ.symmetricAlgebraInvariants] SymmetricAlgebra R M where
  toFun := SymmetricAlgebra.dividedDifference (ρ g) ℓ hσ hℓ
  map_add' := map_add _
  map_smul' a p := by
    rw [Subalgebra.smul_def, RingHom.id_apply, Subalgebra.smul_def]
    -- Every invariant is fixed by `g`, so it passes through the divided difference.
    exact SymmetricAlgebra.dividedDifference_mul_of_map_eq
      ((ρ.symmetricAlgebra_apply g a).symm.trans ((ρ.mem_symmetricAlgebraInvariants a).1 a.2 g)) p

/-- The bundled divided-difference operator of `g` is `SymmetricAlgebra.dividedDifference`. -/
@[simp]
theorem symmetricAlgebraDividedDifference_apply (hσ : ∀ m, m - ρ g m ∈ R ∙ ℓ)
    (hℓ : IsLeftRegular (SymmetricAlgebra.ι R M ℓ)) (p : SymmetricAlgebra R M) :
    ρ.symmetricAlgebraDividedDifference g ℓ hσ hℓ p =
      SymmetricAlgebra.dividedDifference (ρ g) ℓ hσ hℓ p :=
  (rfl)

end CommRing

end Representation
